    "findings": {
      "paper_claim": "prop:li2q-phiq-bar-symmetrization boxed: Li_2^q(z) = \u00bd(log \u03a6_q(z) + log \u03a6_{q\u207b\u00b9}(z)) + O((q-1)\u00b3z)",
      "paper_claim_status": "FALSIFIED \u2014 numerical SUM is identically 0",
      "algebraic_reason": "For Faddeev's \u03a6_q(z) = \u220f_{k\u22650}(1-q^{2k+1}z)^{-1}, the series log \u03a6_q(z) = \u03a3 z^n/n \u00b7 q^n/(1-q^{2n}). Setting q \u2192 q\u207b\u00b9 flips sign of EACH term: q^-n/(1-q^-{2n}) = -q^n/(1-q^{2n}). Therefore log \u03a6_{q\u207b\u00b9}(z) = -log \u03a6_q(z), and the SUM is identically zero. The .md's claimed 'algebraic identity' q^n/(1-q^{2n}) + q^-n/(1-q^-{2n}) = -1/(q^n-q^-n) is an arithmetic error \u2014 the correct value is 0.",
